target/
.git/

# The image builds one crate out of crates/, so nothing below is a build input.
# They were all in the context until now, which cost twice: `COPY . .` shipped
# them to the daemon on every build, and any edit to any of them invalidated the
# `cargo install` layer, so a README or workflow change forced a full recompile
# of the workspace. fuzz/ is 3.6G of corpora on its own and tools/ is 398M of
# build artefacts.
#
# Excluding the Dockerfile is safe: buildx reads it through -f, not out of the
# context, so it is not a file the build can miss.
fuzz/
tools/
# ...except the prerenderer, which Dockerfile.dustnetd installs: a site image
# uses it to turn authored pages into served ones. Its source only — tools/ is
# excluded mostly because of the build artefacts under it, and those are what
# the second line puts back out of reach.
!tools/prerender-figlet/
tools/prerender-figlet/target/
effects/
examples/
docs/
verification/
supply-chain/
.github/
*.md
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dustnetd
.dockerignore
Makefile
